WEBVTT

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:03.950
What did I learn by contributing to the
book on the 5th Pan -African

00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:04.390
Congress?

00:00:07.010 --> 00:00:13.550
Well, one thing clear is the importance of
that Congress, because

00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:18.110
there were four congresses

00:00:18.110 --> 00:00:22.770
before that, as well as Pan -African
conferencing London, and there

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:24.670
have been Pan -African Congresses

00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:24.950
since.

00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:29.070
But the 5th Pan -African Congress in
Manchester was probably the

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:31.190
most important of all of those

00:00:31.190 --> 00:00:32.010
congresses.

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:39.390
It's the one everybody looks back to
today, you know, if you check

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:40.450
out, you know, something

00:00:40.450 --> 00:00:44.170
in the African Union or something, people
will talk about Manchester

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:45.330
Congress, they won't

00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:49.450
talk about the 4th Congress or the 2nd
Congress, but the Manchester

00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:50.850
Congress is very important.

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:55.970
And partly because of when it was held at
the end of the Second World

00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:57.650
War, at a time

00:00:57.650 --> 00:01:03.690
when the whole colonial system was under
threat, where

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:05.210
people in the colonies, especially

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:08.230
Africa and the Caribbean, were kind of
flexing their muscles and

00:01:08.230 --> 00:01:08.990
saying, look, we're not

00:01:08.990 --> 00:01:10.450
going to put up with this anymore.

00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:12.370
We want to be free and independent.

00:01:13.010 --> 00:01:18.130
So the timing was very important, also
because of some of

00:01:18.130 --> 00:01:20.250
the personalities involved, Kwame

00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:24.890
and crewmer, George Padmore, Joe
Mulcanyata, Amy Ashwood Garvey,

00:01:26.290 --> 00:01:27.930
and others, and many, many others.
